## 2. Library Decisions + Reasoning

### 2a. Signature Pad — `react-signature-canvas@1.0.6`

| Candidate | Touch | SVG export | PNG export | Pressure | Bundle | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `react-signature-canvas` | Yes | Via path | `toDataURL('image/png')` | No (not needed) | ~14 KB | **PICK** |
| `signature_pad` (vanilla) | Yes | Via path | Yes | Yes | ~9 KB | Runner-up (no React wrapper) |
| `react-sketchy` | Yes | No | Yes | No | ~22 KB | Overkill |
| `perfect-freehand` + canvas | Yes | Manual | Manual | Yes | ~6 KB | Too manual |

**Why `react-signature-canvas`:** Direct React ref API (`sigPad.getTrimmedCanvas()`, `sigPad.toDataURL()`), production-tested, handles mouse/touch/stylus uniformly, easy to disable/clear/check-empty. SVG export: iterate `_data` property to generate an SVG path string from the stored points array.

**Minimum valid signature:** Check `sigPad.isEmpty()` AND count total points across all strokes `>= 20`. A single dot fails both checks.

**Install:**
```bash
pnpm add react-signature-canvas
pnpm add -D @types/react-signature-canvas
```

### 2b. Drag-Reorder — `@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`

Already the InkOS standard. Use `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy` and `DragOverlay` for the ghost preview. No new install needed if Sprint 3/4 installed them. Verify:
```bash
pnpm list @dnd-kit/core @dnd-kit/sortable
```
If missing: `pnpm add @dnd-kit/core @dnd-kit/sortable @dnd-kit/utilities`

### 2c. Markdown Renderer — `react-markdown` + `rehype-sanitize`

```bash
pnpm add react-markdown rehype-sanitize
```
Used only in section body rendering (template preview + public signing page). Never in the edit form (that's a plain `<Textarea>`). Allowed elements: `p strong em ul ol li a br`. Strip everything else via `rehype-sanitize` with a custom schema.

### 2d. PDF Generation — `@react-pdf/renderer` in BullMQ worker

```bash
# In workers/ package.json only — never in the Next.js app
pnpm add @react-pdf/renderer
```

PDF is generated server-side (worker) after submission. Design: A4 portrait, studio logo top-right, template title as heading, sections rendered in order, signature image embedded as PNG, audit metadata at bottom, watermark "SIGNED COPY — [studio name]" at 5% opacity diagonal. Stored to Supabase Storage `consent-pdfs/[studio_id]/[submission_id].pdf`. Signed URL generated on each download request (1-hour TTL).

**Do NOT use jsPDF or html2canvas.** `@react-pdf/renderer` gives deterministic layout and is worker-safe (no DOM dependency).

### 2e. Date Utilities

`date-fns` is already installed (Sprint 2). New usage: `differenceInYears`, `formatDistanceToNow`, `addYears`, `isBefore`.

### 2f. New shadcn Installs

```bash
# Verify already installed before running
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add resizable   # two-panel split in template builder
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add toggle      # section type palette active state
```

All other needed primitives (Tabs, DataTable, Dialog, Sheet, Button, Badge, Skeleton, Tooltip, AlertDialog, ScrollArea, Switch, Select, Input, Textarea, Separator, Popover, Command, DropdownMenu) confirmed from Sprints 1–4.

