**Version save logic (UI rule):**

- If only metadata changed (name, kind, retention_years, is_default, language, required_for_booking, requires_guardian) AND sections are unchanged → `PATCH /api/consent-templates/[id]` (no new version)
- If any section changed (add/remove/reorder/edit) → `POST /api/consent-templates/[id]/versions` (creates new version, increments version number)
- Toast: "Template saved (v{n})" or "New version created (v{n})"

